<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
{# Redirect stub — Thematic Baskets merged into Sector Intelligence (sector_central.html).
   Pattern: vector_allocation.html.j2 (noindex + meta refresh + canonical to the TARGET via
   seo_path + location.replace). The 47 basket detail pages (site/basket/*) stay live.
   #theme-<id> hashes must FORWARD to the merged page, whose resolveThemeHash() routes them
   to basket/<id>.html — alert rows live ~90d and bookmarks longer, so inbound
   baskets.html#theme-<id> links outlast this page (tests/test_theme_hash_deeplink.py). #}
{% set seo_title = "Thematic Baskets moved into Sector Intelligence — Mastermind" %}
{% set seo_desc = "The 47 equal-weight theme baskets — action lanes, rotation map and performance — now live inside the US Sector Intelligence page." %}
{% set seo_path = "sector_central.html" %}
{% include "_seo_head.html.j2" %}
<title>Thematic Baskets moved into Sector Intelligence — Mastermind</title>
<meta name="robots" content="noindex,follow">
{# THEME DEEP-LINK RESOLVER. Emitters still link baskets.html#theme-<id> (alerts rows —
   engine/alert_triage.py assembles page+anchor — plus bookmarks and outbound marketing
   links). This stub is the RECEIVER: a bare redirect discards the hash and dumps the
   visitor at the lanes anchor, which is how the contract regressed. Resolve to the
   theme's own detail page instead. Runs before the meta refresh is parsed so the
   redirect can never win the race. `theme_ids` is the nightly basket id list from
   build_baskets.py — the same ids build_theme_detail writes basket/<id>.html for, so a
   stale id falls through to the merged page instead of becoming a 404. #}
<script>
window.__THEME_IDS={{ theme_ids | default([]) | tojson }};
function themeById(id){return (window.__THEME_IDS||[]).indexOf(id)<0?null:id}
function resolveThemeHash(){
var id=themeById(location.hash.slice(7));
if(id){window.__THEME_RESOLVED=1;location.replace('basket/'+id+'.html');return}
location.replace("sector_central.html#actnow-section");
}
if(location.hash.startsWith('#theme-'))resolveThemeHash();
</script>
<meta http-equiv="refresh" content="0;url=sector_central.html#actnow-section">
<style>body{margin:0;min-height:100vh;display:grid;place-items:center;background:#0c0f16;color:#edf0f7;font:15px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{width:min(560px,calc(100% - 40px));padding:32px;border:1px solid #2a3040;border-radius:14px}h1{margin:0 0 10px;font-size:25px}p{color:#aab1c1}a{color:#a895ff}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
<h1>Thematic Baskets now live in Sector Intelligence</h1>
<p>The 47 equal-weight theme baskets — the action lanes, the rotation map and the performance explorer — merged into one page with the sector cycle map and the whole-market rotation desk.</p>
<p><a href="sector_central.html#actnow-section">Open Sector Intelligence →</a></p>
</main>
<script>
if(location.hash&&location.hash.startsWith('#theme-')){location.replace('sector_central.html'+location.hash)}
else{location.replace("sector_central.html#actnow-section")}
</script>
</body>
</html>
